.TH NYX-MACSPOOF 8 "2025" "NYX Framework" "NYX Phobos Tools"
.SH NAME
nyx-macspoof \- MAC address spoofing utility
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nyx-macspoof
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nyx-macspoof
modifies MAC addresses on network interfaces. It supports setting
a specific address, generating a random locally-administered unicast
MAC, and restoring the original hardware address.
.PP
When launched, it enters an interactive shell with line editing,
tab completion, and command history. Type
.B help
for available commands.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.BI show " -i iface"
Display the current MAC address of an interface.
.TP
.BI random " -i iface"
Generate and apply a random MAC address. The original is backed up.
.TP
.BI set " -i iface -m mac"
Set a specific MAC address in XX:XX:XX:XX:XX:XX format.
.TP
.BI restore " -i iface"
Restore the original (permanent) MAC address from backup.
.TP
.B list
List all network interfaces with MAC, IP, netmask, and state.
.TP
.B help
Show available commands and usage.
.TP
.B exit
Exit the shell.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
sudo nyx-macspoof
macspoof> list
macspoof> show -i eth0
macspoof> random -i eth0
macspoof> set -i eth0 -m 00:11:22:33:44:55
macspoof> restore -i eth0
macspoof> exit
.fi
.SH NOTES
This tool requires root privileges (network interface configuration).
When launched without root from a terminal, it will attempt to
re-execute itself with sudo.
